# ==============================================================================
# DOCKER BUILD CONTEXT FILTER
# ==============================================================================
# Context root = ./playground (the Go module root). The Dockerfile depends on
# `COPY go.mod go.sum ./`, then `COPY . .`, then `go build ./cmd/server`.
#
# ⛔ NEVER ignore: go.mod, go.sum, cmd/, internal/, pkg/
#    (nothing below matches those paths)
#
# Everything that survives this file is uploaded to the builder and baked into
# the intermediate `builder` stage layer, which is retrievable from the image.
# Patterns are context-root relative. A bare `*.ext` matches ONLY files at the
# root — use `**/` to reach subdirectories. To re-include a path inside an
# ignored directory, re-include the directory as well (or ignore `dir/*`).
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# VERSION CONTROL METADATA
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.gitmodules
.github/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONTAINER / ORCHESTRATION DEFINITIONS
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# The daemon always receives the Dockerfile out-of-band and COPY/ADD never copy
# these, so excluding them is safe and keeps the `COPY . .` cache key clean.
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
docker-compose*.yaml
compose*.yml
compose*.yaml
.docker/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# EDITOR / OS NOISE
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# DOCUMENTATION & HOST-LEVEL TOOLING
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime is `scratch` + a static binary: no doc ever ships.
# NOTE: drop **/*.md if you ever add `//go:embed` of markdown assets.
**/*.md
docs/
notes/
# NOTE: remove this line if the Dockerfile ever switches to `RUN make build`.
Makefile

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCALLY COMPILED ARTIFACTS
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# `go build ./cmd/server` without -o drops an ~8MB `server` binary here;
# the book's appendix Makefile writes ./bin/microservice. Root-anchored
# patterns only — cmd/server/ is NOT affected by the `server` entry.
server
bin/
dist/
build/
*.exe
*.test
*.out
coverage.out
*.coverprofile
*.prof

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS & LOCAL RUNTIME STATE
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Without this block, `COPY . .` bakes real credentials into the builder stage.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
secrets/
logs/
**/*.log
tmp/
data/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.sql

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# GO BUILD / MODULE CACHES (only if redirected into the project)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
.cache/
.gocache/
go-build*/

# ⚠️ DO NOT ignore vendor/ : with go >= 1.14 a vendor/ directory silently turns
#    on -mod=vendor, so excluding it would break `go build` in the container.
